			"route": { "family": "Lexeme", "kind": "VERB" },
			"notes": {
				"rationale": "The Vorsitzende asks for quiet: bitten um is the plain verb, Duden bitten 1 (darf ich um Aufmerksamkeit bitten!) and DWDS bitten 1a (der Redner bittet … um Ruhe). Duden and DWDS list the formula darf ich bitten? only without an object, as an invitation to dance, so with the object um Ruhe and a sense the formula lacks the words resolve word by word (de/routine-formula-is-intj, ruled on #828, case 6). um is governed by bitten, a member recorded in valencyEvidence as um + Acc and kept out of the normalized Surface bitten, as in sie-wurde-um-geduld-gebeten (de/governed-preposition-joins-its-governor). bitten is the infinitive Darf governs.",
				"knownMistakes": [
					"Grouping Darf ich … bitten as the Locution INTJ darf ich bitten with um Ruhe free: the formula takes no object, and here the words mean only their sum."
				]
			},
